TI  - Machine learning algorithms for medical image security
PY  - 2020
T2  - Intelligent Data Security Solutions for e-Health Applications
SP  - 169
EP  - 183
DO  - 10.1016/B978-0-12-819511-6.00009-1
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85126893127?origin=resultslist
AB  - Expectations for artificial intelligence are increasing day by day with the evolution of machine learning techniques. In recent years, machine learning has shown an increased ability to build security applications. Exceptionally high accuracy is achieved when machine learning is used for data-driven problems such as classification of malware, intrusion detection, securing health prediction systems, autonomous security audits from system logs, etc. Key challenges in adopting machine learning algorithms for security and safety critical areas include lack of transparency, inadequate vulnerability analysis, etc. Many machine learning algorithms for security and privacy are developed with little or no understanding of the underlying security aspects. Malicious external influences can cause the machine learning algorithm to predict falsely or misclassify, which might create a huge impact on security and life critical applications. The efficiency of machine learning algorithms often relies on huge volumes of data, which involves sensitive information as well. It is a greater challenge not to expose the privacy of sensitive data. This chapter addresses the impact of machine learning algorithms for applications involving medical image security. © 2020 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
