AU  - Patwari, A.K.
AU  - Reddy, G.V.R.
TI  - A Robust and High Quality Steganography Method with Attack Resistant Ability for Hiding Medical Images Using Deformable Attention-Based Conv-Transformer
PY  - 2026
T2  - Lecture Notes in Networks and Systems
VL  - 2019 LNNS
SP  - 576
EP  - 595
DO  - 10.1007/978-3-032-28304-7_48
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047319493?origin=resultslist
AB  - Steganography has recently been popular in medical image transmission, as it has a lot of patient-specific and sensitive information. A lot of medical data has been gathered for research purposes; however, most patient records are leaked along with medical images. Recent steganography techniques developed for the medical sector aim for both security and image quality, as some image hiding processes can lead to the disruption of original critical details. Medical steganography is more complex than other platforms, as the medical records are more complex, and it is essential to ensure critical diagnostic details are not altered. It is also vulnerable to various diseases, as specific attacks like image cropping can sufficiently damage the embedded image, and hence, defining robust steganographic techniques is necessary to support secure medical data transmission. In this work, an attention-based deep learning model is proposed for securing the medical images during the transmission process. The required medical images of the patient are collected from reputable sources. Then, the Deformable Attention-based Conv-Transformer (DA-ConvT) is proposed for executing the medical image steganography. The DA-CT model uses the cover image and input images for analyzing the stego image. Moreover, the secret bits will be hidden in the medical images using the proposed DA-CT. In addition, the DA-CT-based stenography is used to transmit medical images securely, preventing changes that could compromise the accuracy of the disease diagnosis process. Finally, several experimental tests are conducted to prove the effectiveness of the proposed method over conventional algorithms. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
